The live failure this whole project was filed from, byte for byte: a listing that
reached the catalogue through the correct zero-touch path because nothing in the
system had ever asked what language a listing was in.

This is a SCRIPT check, not a language detector. It catches a card written
entirely in another alphabet and cannot tell English from French — and it says so
in its own last paragraph, because a gate that overstates its reach is one people
route around.
